<%# locals: (heading:, standfirst:) %>
<%#
  Page furniture for a published legal document (WS-C). /terms and /privacy are
  the same page with different prose — same marketing nav, same "Legal" kicker
  and standfirst, same reading-measure `.legal` article, same colophon — so the
  chrome lives here once and each document file is just its own text. It is a
  partial LAYOUT: the documents render it with a block, and the block is what
  lands inside `<article class="legal">`.

  The "last updated" line deliberately stays in each document rather than moving
  here: the two are amended separately, so one shared date would be a claim we
  couldn't keep true.
%>
<% content_for :title, "#{heading} — Stablemate" %>

<%= render "nav" %>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap sec-intro">
    <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="flow h2"><%= heading %></h1>
    <p class="sub"><%= standfirst %></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="legal">
      <%= yield %>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<%= render "colophon" %>
